          "guid": "mrwv1siz8w8c7btt",
          "message": {
            "text": "O4 flips the `codex_interactive_permissions` default: absent now means the **overlay is ON** (`!== false`), where the HS-9359 exec drive treated absent as auto-approve. Behavior change for existing codex projects is intentional (maintainer decision) — the spike showed `approvalPolicy: 'untrusted'` only escalates genuinely unsafe actions, so popup noise stays low. `skills.ts::ensureCodexHooks` still gates on `=== true` (hooks are legacy, only for manual `codex --enable hooks` runs); the client checkbox default was flipped in `settingsDialog.tsx` to match.\n",
            "markdown": "O4 flips the `codex_interactive_permissions` default: absent now means the **overlay is ON** (`!== false`), where the HS-9359 exec drive treated absent as auto-approve. Behavior change for existing codex projects is intentional (maintainer decision) — the spike showed `approvalPolicy: 'untrusted'` only escalates genuinely unsafe actions, so popup noise stays low. `skills.ts::ensureCodexHooks` still gates on `=== true` (hooks are legacy, only for manual `codex --enable hooks` runs); the client checkbox default was flipped in `settingsDialog.tsx` to match.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/codexAppServer.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 39,
                  "endLine": 43,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/** HS-9359 / HS-9383 (O4) — route codex approvals through the §47 overlay. Default is\n *  now ON (absent ⇒ overlay); explicit `false` ⇒ auto-approve in the bridge. */\nexport function codexInteractivePermissions(dataDir: string): boolean {\n  return readFileSettings(dataDir).codex_interactive_permissions !== false;\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
