          "guid": "mrx6ceh8pwguk7g8",
          "message": {
            "text": "The **live-stdio-session veto** is the load-bearing condition here, not an optimization: codex rollout files are single-writer. If the drive's session runs on the private stdio child (daemon was unreachable at boot), that child's core owns the rollout — a TUI attaching through the *daemon* would resume the same rollout in a second core, and both would append to one JSONL. So the attach is only emitted when the live session is on the daemon transport, or there is no live session and the daemon socket exists (the next session will prefer daemon). The rollout-file-existence check is equally deliberate: `codex resume` fails \"no rollout found\" until the thread's first turn persists (HS-9386 finding), so `existsSync(rolloutPath)` is exactly the \"attach will work\" predicate — not a heuristic.\n",
            "markdown": "The **live-stdio-session veto** is the load-bearing condition here, not an optimization: codex rollout files are single-writer. If the drive's session runs on the private stdio child (daemon was unreachable at boot), that child's core owns the rollout — a TUI attaching through the *daemon* would resume the same rollout in a second core, and both would append to one JSONL. So the attach is only emitted when the live session is on the daemon transport, or there is no live session and the daemon socket exists (the next session will prefer daemon). The rollout-file-existence check is equally deliberate: `codex resume` fails \"no rollout found\" until the thread's first turn persists (HS-9386 finding), so `existsSync(rolloutPath)` is exactly the \"attach will work\" predicate — not a heuristic.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/codexAppServer.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 193,
                  "endLine": 207,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export function codexTerminalAttachCommand(dataDir: string, deps: AttachCommandDeps = {}): string | null {\n  if (!isCodexAppServerEnabled()) return null;\n  const persisted = readPersistedCodexThread(dataDir);\n  if (persisted === null || persisted.rolloutPath === null) return null;\n  const fileExists = deps.fileExists ?? existsSync;\n  if (!fileExists(persisted.rolloutPath)) return null;\n  const socketPath = deps.socketPath ?? codexDaemonSocketPath();\n  const live = sessions.get(dataDir);\n  if (live !== undefined && !live.finished && live.transport !== null) {\n    if (live.transport.kind !== 'daemon') return null; // stdio session owns the rollout\n  } else if (!fileExists(socketPath)) {\n    return null; // no daemon to attach to (the drive would start one on next play)\n  }\n  // Single-quote the URL — home directories can contain spaces.\n  return `codex resume ${persisted.threadId} --remote 'unix://${socketPath}'`;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
