          "guid": "mrx6cenyk137gdjr",
          "message": {
            "text": "Shared-thread interplay was live-verified on codex-cli 0.145.0 (pty-driven TUI + headless daemon driver on one thread) before wiring the terminal attach: (1) a `turn/start` sent while another client's turn is in flight is **accepted and queued server-side** by codex — it ran after the active turn with no rejection and no interleaving, so the drive needs no thread-busy awareness; (2) an unsubmitted TUI draft survives a driven turn rendering above it; (3) TUI-typed turns stream to the drive's connection (they land in the Commands Log transcript, and the HS-9388 phase-guard keeps them from flipping Hot Sheet busy/done). See also `src/terminals/resolveCommand.ts` (the consuming resolution) and docs/123 §123.4.\n",
            "markdown": "Shared-thread interplay was live-verified on codex-cli 0.145.0 (pty-driven TUI + headless daemon driver on one thread) before wiring the terminal attach: (1) a `turn/start` sent while another client's turn is in flight is **accepted and queued server-side** by codex — it ran after the active turn with no rejection and no interleaving, so the drive needs no thread-busy awareness; (2) an unsubmitted TUI draft survives a driven turn rendering above it; (3) TUI-typed turns stream to the drive's connection (they land in the Commands Log transcript, and the HS-9388 phase-guard keeps them from flipping Hot Sheet busy/done). See also `src/terminals/resolveCommand.ts` (the consuming resolution) and docs/123 §123.4.\n"
          },
