          "guid": "ms2w014pk4xauhcm",
          "message": {
            "text": "Dropping the \"rollout exists on disk\" precondition here is a deliberate behavior change, not collateral of the deletion.\n\nThat check was a model-A precondition: the terminal used to launch codex resume <driveThreadId> --remote, and codex resume fails -32600 no rollout found until a turn has persisted a rollout JSONL — so pre-starting the daemon before that point bought nothing.\n\nModel-B's launch is codex --remote … -C <projectDir>, which mints a fresh thread and only needs the socket. Keeping the rollout gate would have meant a brand-new codex project never pre-starts the daemon, so its first terminal open pays the cold start (codexTerminalNeedsDaemonEnsure awaits ensureCodexDaemonRunning inline). Now it doesn't.\n\nThe gate that replaces it is codexDriveDiscoverEnabled() — with model-B off there is no daemon-hosted launch to serve, so the pre-start correctly no-ops and the drive starts the daemon itself at play time, exactly as before.\n",
            "markdown": "Dropping the \"rollout exists on disk\" precondition here is a deliberate behavior change, not collateral of the deletion.\n\nThat check was a **model-A** precondition: the terminal used to launch `codex resume <driveThreadId> --remote`, and `codex resume` fails `-32600 no rollout found` until a turn has persisted a rollout JSONL — so pre-starting the daemon before that point bought nothing.\n\nModel-B's launch is `codex --remote … -C <projectDir>`, which mints a **fresh** thread and only needs the socket. Keeping the rollout gate would have meant a brand-new codex project never pre-starts the daemon, so its first terminal open pays the cold start (`codexTerminalNeedsDaemonEnsure` awaits `ensureCodexDaemonRunning` inline). Now it doesn't.\n\nThe gate that replaces it is `codexDriveDiscoverEnabled()` — with model-B off there is no daemon-hosted launch to serve, so the pre-start correctly no-ops and the drive starts the daemon itself at play time, exactly as before.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/codexAppServer.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 220,
                  "endLine": 227,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export function prestartCodexDaemonIfNeeded(dataDir: string, deps: PrestartDeps = {}): void {\n  if (!codexDriveDiscoverEnabled() || !isCodexAppServerEnabled()) return;\n  const tool = readFileSettings(dataDir).ai_tool;\n  if (typeof tool !== 'string' || tool.trim().toLowerCase() !== 'codex') return;\n  const fileExists = deps.fileExists ?? existsSync;\n  if (fileExists(deps.socketPath ?? codexDaemonSocketPath())) return; // already up\n  void (deps.ensureDaemon ?? ensureCodexDaemonRunning)().catch(() => { /* best-effort — plain codex fallback stands */ });\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
