          "guid": "ms2xabyroqli7wsf",
          "message": {
            "text": "turnEndsOnStatus is a per-TURN snapshot rather than a live read of session.subscribed, and that distinction is the whole reason the mid-turn resubscribe is safe.\n\nThe obvious implementation — leave the idle branch gated on !session.subscribed — breaks on a specific interleave. The mid-turn resume can land after the daemon broadcast turn/completed (which we didn't receive, being unsubscribed at the time) but before the idle that follows it. With a live read, we'd then ignore that idle because we're now \"subscribed\", and nothing else would end the turn: busy sticks until the client's 60s fallback.\n\nSnapshotting at turn start makes the resubscribe purely additive. The turn ends the way it was always going to end; the turn/completed the new subscription also delivers finds phase !== 'active' and no-ops. Measured ordering that this relies on: the daemon emits idle before turn/completed (docs/129 §129.9).\n",
            "markdown": "`turnEndsOnStatus` is a per-TURN snapshot rather than a live read of `session.subscribed`, and that distinction is the whole reason the mid-turn resubscribe is safe.\n\nThe obvious implementation — leave the idle branch gated on `!session.subscribed` — breaks on a specific interleave. The mid-turn resume can land *after* the daemon broadcast `turn/completed` (which we didn't receive, being unsubscribed at the time) but *before* the `idle` that follows it. With a live read, we'd then ignore that idle because we're now \"subscribed\", and nothing else would end the turn: busy sticks until the client's 60s fallback.\n\nSnapshotting at turn start makes the resubscribe purely additive. The turn ends the way it was always going to end; the `turn/completed` the new subscription also delivers finds `phase !== 'active'` and no-ops. Measured ordering that this relies on: the daemon emits `idle` *before* `turn/completed` (docs/129 §129.9).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/codexAppServer.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 178,
                  "endLine": 190,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  currentTurnId: string | null;\n  /** HS-9439 — how the CURRENT turn ends, decided when it starts: true ⇒ from\n   *  `thread/status/changed` idle (we were unsubscribed at turn start, so no\n   *  `turn/completed` was coming). Deliberately a per-TURN snapshot rather than a\n   *  live read of `subscribed`: the mid-turn resubscribe below can flip `subscribed`\n   *  while this turn runs, and switching the ending rule mid-flight opens a window\n   *  where the turn ends by neither rule (subscribed just after `turn/completed` was\n   *  broadcast, but before the idle we'd then ignore) and busy sticks. */\n  turnEndsOnStatus: boolean;\n  /** HS-9439 — pending mid-turn `thread/resume` retry, cleared on teardown. */\n  midTurnSubscribeTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null;\n  /** 'booting' until the handshake + thread setup completes; then idle/active. */\n  phase: 'booting' | 'idle' | 'active';"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
